  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 73ff519377b990a4c81cd1461a3c1f62, type: 3}
  m_Name: Kalaw_W03_Teach
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueNode
  speakerName: Kalaw
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: e9a1f2822809deb49a0ce098da0fddca, type: 3}
  dialogueText: 'No damagen ka iti ''kumusta ka?'', mabalinmo nga ibaga no kumusta
    ti kasasaadmo.


    Iti Ilokano, ti ''nasayaat ak'' ket kayatna a saoen ti ''I''m
    fine'' wenno ''nasayaat ti kasasaadko.''


    Kas pagarigan, no damagen ka no
    kasano ti panagdaliasatmo, mabalinmo nga sumungbat iti ''Nasayaat ak.''


    Denggem
    a naimbag: nasayaat ak.


    Ita, padasem nga ibagam ti ''nasayaat ak'' iti
    bukodmo a timek.'
  translatedText: 'When someone asks you ''kumusta ka?'', you can tell them how you''re
    doing.

    In Ilokano, ''nasayaat ak'' means ''I''m fine'' or ''I''m doing well.''

    For
    example, if someone asks how your journey is going, you can answer: ''Nasayaat
    ak.''

    Now, try saying ''nasayaat ak'' yourself.'
